---
// Technical architecture and engineering breakdown in pure Vercel light design style
---

<section id="architecture" class="py-16 md:py-24 border-t border-[#ebebeb] bg-white">
  <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
    <div class="max-w-3xl mb-12">
      <span class="mono-eyebrow text-[#0070f3] block mb-2">Technical Architecture</span>
      <h2 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-[#171717] mb-4">
        Engineered for real-time inference on consumer CPUs.
      </h2>
      <p class="text-base text-[#4d4d4d] leading-relaxed">
        Kyutai’s Pocket TTS is a 100M parameter model family combining continuous audio flow matching with Mimi’s acoustic representations, packaged into quantized ONNX graphs for client-side WebAssembly execution.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- 4-Card Grid (Vercel hairline cards) -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-6">
      <!-- Card 1 -->
      <div class="vercel-card rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-[#f2f2f2] flex items-center justify-center text-[#171717] mb-4">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <rect width="18" height="18" x="3" y="3" rx="2" />
            <path d="M3 9h18M9 21V9" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <span class="mono-eyebrow text-[#8f8f8f]">100M Flow Matching LM</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#171717]">Continuous Audio Language Modeling</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] leading-relaxed">
          Unlike discrete token speech synthesizers that suffer from high latency, Pocket TTS uses continuous latent flow matching. This achieves natural prosody and voice inflections in only 1–2 ODE steps per audio frame.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 2 -->
      <div class="vercel-card rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-[#f2f2f2] flex items-center justify-center text-[#171717] mb-4">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M12 2v20M17 5v14M7 8v8M22 10v4M2 10v4" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <span class="mono-eyebrow text-[#8f8f8f]">Kyutai Mimi Codec</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#171717]">24kHz High-Fidelity Audio Compression</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] leading-relaxed">
          Mimi compresses 24,000&nbsp;Hz waveforms into 32-dimensional continuous latent representations. It functions as both the acoustic feature extractor during voice cloning and the neural vocoder during speech synthesis.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 3 -->
      <div class="vercel-card rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-[#f2f2f2] flex items-center justify-center text-[#171717] mb-4">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M4 17l6-6-6-6M12 19h8" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <span class="mono-eyebrow text-[#8f8f8f]">WebAssembly & SIMD</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#171717]">Client-Side ONNX Runtime Web</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] leading-relaxed">
          Executing via INT8 quantization in WebAssembly with multi-threaded SIMD instructions. The model runs at 4x–8x real-time on standard laptops without requiring a discrete graphics card or GPU acceleration.
        </p>
      </div>

      <!-- Card 4 -->
      <div class="vercel-card rounded-xl p-6 sm:p-8 space-y-3">
        <div class="w-10 h-10 rounded-lg bg-[#f2f2f2] flex items-center justify-center text-[#171717] mb-4">
          <svg class="w-5 h-5" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M20 13c0 5-3.5 7.5-7.66 8.95a1 1 0 0 1-.67-.01C7.5 20.5 4 18 4 13V6a1 1 0 0 1 1-1c2 0 4.5-1.2 6.24-2.72a1.17 1.17 0 0 1 1.52 0C14.51 3.81 17 5 19 5a1 1 0 0 1 1 1z" />
          </svg>
        </div>
        <span class="mono-eyebrow text-[#8f8f8f]">Local Privacy & Consent</span>
        <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold text-[#171717]">Zero Cloud Telemetry & Consent Gate</h3>
        <p class="text-sm text-[#4d4d4d] leading-relaxed">
          All audio recordings, cloned speaker profiles, and generated speech remain strictly in your browser’s volatile memory and CacheStorage. An explicit speaker permission confirmation is enforced before cloning.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Code Pipeline Diagram in Vercel Clean Light Code Style -->
    <div class="mt-8 rounded-xl bg-[#f6f8fa] border border-[#ebebeb] p-5 text-xs font-mono text-[#24292f] overflow-x-auto shadow-2xs">
      <div class="flex items-center space-x-2 text-[#8f8f8f] mb-3 border-b border-[#ebebeb] pb-2 text-[11px]">
        <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#ff5f56]"></span>
        <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#ffbd2e]"></span>
        <span class="w-2.5 h-2.5 rounded-full bg-[#27c93f]"></span>
        <span class="ml-2 text-[#57606a]">client-inference-flow.ts</span>
      </div>
      <pre class="leading-relaxed"><code><span class="text-[#6e7781]">// 1. Audio Conditioning / Voice Cloning</span>
<span class="text-[#cf222e]">const</span> speakerEmbeddings = <span class="text-[#cf222e]">await</span> mimiEncoder.run(&#123; audio: referenceAudio24kHz &#125;);

<span class="text-[#6e7781]">// 2. Text Conditioning (SentencePiece + Tokenizer)</span>
<span class="text-[#cf222e]">const</span> textEmbeddings = <span class="text-[#cf222e]">await</span> textConditioner.run(&#123; token_ids: tokenIds &#125;);

<span class="text-[#6e7781]">// 3. Flow Matching Velocity ODE Step</span>
<span class="text-[#cf222e]">const</span> audioLatents = <span class="text-[#cf222e]">await</span> flowLmMain.run(&#123; text_embeddings, speakerEmbeddings, ...state &#125;);

<span class="text-[#6e7781]">// 4. Mimi Neural Decoder Waveform Synthesis</span>
<span class="text-[#cf222e]">const</span> waveform24k = <span class="text-[#cf222e]">await</span> mimiDecoder.run(&#123; latent: audioLatents &#125;);
<span class="text-[#1a7f37]">pcmPlayer.playAudio(waveform24k); // ~200ms latency to first audio sample</span></code></pre>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
